Channels pass values between goroutines. Create one with chan T: fn main() { ch := chan int{} go fn (ch chan int) { ch <- 42 }(ch) result := <-ch println(result)
} An unbuffered channel blocks on send until a receiver is ready. A buffered channel has a capacity and does not block until full: fn main() { ch := chan int{cap: 3} ch <- 1 ch <- 2 ch <- 3 println(<-ch) println(<-ch) println(<-ch)
} Channel direction restricts how a channel can be used. chan<- T is send-only, <-chan T is receive-only: fn sender(ch chan<- int) { ch <- 42
} fn receiver(ch <-chan int) { val := <-ch println(val)
} fn main() { ch := chan int{} go sender(ch) receiver(ch)
}

